Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Postmarks Scrape the Bone
- Story & Context: During the bitter December 2004 eviction of the squatters' workshop behind Todmorden Station, Parveen Chana scrambled through drifting snow to salvage his hand-carved copper bayan from private bailiffs. In the melee, a 19th-century French regulator clock was kicked down the iron stairwell, its brass gears scattering across wet cobblestones and wedging into a jagged slab of Campo del Cielo meteorite that Parveen used as a drum tuning anvil. Reeking of machine oil and damp soot, he scraped an iron escapement wheel across the skin of the tabla while the bailiffs smashed the windows above, unleashing a pitch-bending, metallic resonance that caused the police dogs to sit and whine instead of attack. From that night’s panic came the genre’s opening decree: "You stamped the date upon my throat, but the train had already burned."
