Track 2: Sister Leocadia's Returned Airmail
- Story & Context: In the moldering sub-basement of a deconsecrated convent in Hebden Bridge, Evelyn Vesper unsealed an iron-banded post box that had languished unclaimed since the winter freeze of 1973. Breathing the sour musk of rotten parchment and curdled envelope gum, she sorted through ninety unforwarded letters penned to a runaway novice named Sister Leocadia, each detailing small domestic heresies and frantic apologies that arrived decades too late. Strung out on cold black tea and sleepless grief, Evelyn wired a disassembled turret-clock escapement directly into the bridge of her bass VI, using a razor-thin wafer of Gibeon meteorite to ground the hum as she spoke-sang the forgotten confessions into a ribbon mic. Her baritone drawl echoed into the damp stone: "Every promise in this envelope rusted before the border opened."
